  "notes": "Boot a Diner ROM from a fresh state directory holding only the .nv file written by diner-nvram-init, with three balls in the trough (11-13 closed) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Coin up one credit and start a game, then play three balls with a modelled serve and drain: wait for the shooter lane feeder (22), move a ball from the trough to the shooter lane and plunge it, close playfield switches 19 and 20, and drain it to the outhole until the outhole kicker (1) fires. Ball 1 is tilted with three plumb-bob pulses (public 1) before it drains. Public 23 is s11.c's S11_GAMEONSOL. Output checkpoints require a transition at 23 from the start press, from the third tilt pulse, before ball 2 is served and after ball 3 drains, and a coil at every serve and drain, so the run fails if the game does not progress; they accept a transition in either direction, so the direction of each one is read from the trace.",
